E18 reviews/receipts/20261020-p4-apply/evidence/18-launchagent-template-throttleinterval-12.template
1: <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
2: <!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
3: <!--
4:   The one local OTLP collector for this MacBook.
5: 
6:   Agents post to 127.0.0.1:4320 and hold no vendor key. This job reads the SigNoz
7:   ingestion key from 1Password at run time, drops any span group with no
8:   service.name, refuses the ChatGPT app's codex-worker, rate guards each service
9:   separately, and sends to SigNoz while mirroring named spans to Langfuse for the
10:   side by side day.
11: 
12:   Interpreter is /usr/bin/python3 (3.9.6) deliberately, matching the existing relay
13:   job: the collector is stdlib only and its test suite passes on both 3.9.6 and
14:   3.14.6, so it does not depend on a Homebrew Python that an update could move.
15: 
16:   Verified before install, 2026-10-20:
17:     the 1Password robot read works with a launchd shaped environment and no TTY
18:     (keychain exit 0, op read exit 0); SIGTERM shuts the collector down cleanly and
19:     flushes its final counts to stdout, which launchd captures in the log below.
20: 
21:   AFTER THE SIDE BY SIDE DAY: delete the two argument entries that say "upstream"
22:   and "langfuse" from the array below, leaving the SigNoz pair, then reload the job.
23:   SigNoz is then the only destination.
24: 
25:   NOTE on this comment: XML forbids a double hyphen inside a comment, so flag names
26:   are written here without their leading dashes. plutil lint accepts a file that
27:   breaks that rule but plistlib rejects it, which is how the mistake was caught.
28: 
29:   ThrottleInterval is 120 rather than the usual 10. On 2026-10-20 a crash loop at a
30:   10 second interval exhausted the shared 1Password service account for every agent
31:   on this machine. The collector no longer exits when a key read fails, so the loop
32:   should not recur, but the longer interval is the second line of defence.
33: 
34:   Install, uninstall and proof: work/signoz-relay/APPLY-p4.md in
35:   ~/Projects/alex-system-map.
36: -->
37: <plist version="1.0">
38: <dict>
39:     <key>Label</key>
40:     <string>com.alex.signoz-collector</string>
41:     <key>ProgramArguments</key>
42:     <array>
43:         <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
44:         <string>-B</string>
45:         <string><HOME>/Projects/alex-system-map/tools/otel_collector.py</string>
46:         <string>--port</string>
47:         <string>4320</string>
48:         <string>--upstream</string>
49:         <string>signoz</string>
50:         <string>--upstream</string>
51:         <string>langfuse</string>
52:         <string>--log</string>
53:         <string><HOME>/.agents/runtime/otel-collector.jsonl</string>
54:     </array>
55:     <key>RunAtLoad</key>
56:     <true/>
57:     <key>KeepAlive</key>
58:     <true/>
59:     <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
60:     <integer>120</integer>
61:     <key>StandardOutPath</key>
62:     <string><HOME>/.agents/runtime/signoz-collector.out.log</string>
63:     <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
64:     <string><HOME>/.agents/runtime/signoz-collector.err.log</string>
65:     <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
66:     <string><HOME>/Projects/alex-system-map</string>
67: </dict>
68: </plist>

